  "problem": "Let $Q$ be an orthogonal linear transformation. Which of the following are orthogonal sets?\n\nI. $U=\\{Q([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]),Q([\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}])\\}$\n\nII. $V=\\{Q([\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]),Q([\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}]),Q([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}])\\}$\n\nIII. $W=\\{Q([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]),Q([\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}])\\}$",
